Imports: dplyr,MASS,mvtnorm,spdep,SCDA,stats,geodist,sf
Description: Estimation of hierarchical spatio-temporal models using the Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm within a likelihood-based framework.
    Technical details are available in Fassò, Cameletti and Nicolis (2007) <doi:10.1002/env.837>, Fassò and Cameletti (2010) <doi:10.1177/0037549709102150>, and McLachlan and Krishnan (2008, ISBN:9780470191613).
    Estimation of the parameters is performed via maximum likelihood (ML).
    Standard errors and prediction (spatial mapping) uncertainty are computed using a spatio-temporal parametric bootstrap.
    The package also introduces an extended version of STEM models, namely the spatially-clustered STEM (SC-STEM), which allows regression parameters to be spatially varying according to a cluster-wise structure.
    SC-STEM models are based on the methodology proposed by Sugasawa and Murakami (2021) <doi:10.1016/j.spasta.2021.100525> and Cerqueti, Maranzano and Mattera (2024) <https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.15874>.
